+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: ruzstd (KillingSpark/zstd-rs)
+
+## 1. Summary
+
+Added 9 hegel properties to `ruzstd/src/tests/mod.rs` (module `tests::hegel_props`),
+targeting the decoder — ruzstd's core purpose is *decoding* Zstandard, so the
+`zstd` C-bindings crate (already a dev-dependency for the existing interop
+tests) is used as the reference encoder/decoder oracle. All properties pass at
+the default case count and at a 10x exploratory run (1000 cases each, verified
+live via case counters). **No bugs found** — consistent with the crate being
+continuously fuzzed (six libFuzzer targets including a differential interop
+target against libzstd).
+
+Maintainer AI policy: `ruzstd/Readme.md` has an "AI Contributions" section that
+*permits* AI-created contributions provided a human reads/verifies them before
+submitting a PR and handles all PR communication. Nothing here has been (or may
+be) upstreamed without that human review; nothing was pushed.
+
+Setup: `cargo add --dev hegeltest -p ruzstd` (hegeltest 0.28.2). The crate is
+`#![no_std]` + edition 2018, so the test module needs `extern crate std;`,
+`use std::{format, string::ToString};` and `use alloc::{vec, vec::Vec};`, and
+`assert!` messages must pass format arguments explicitly. `.hegel/` added to
+`.gitignore`.
+
+## 2. Properties Added
+
+All in `ruzstd/src/tests/mod.rs`, `mod hegel_props` (std feature only, since
+the reference oracle needs std). Shared generators: `payloads()` (empty /
+random-incompressible / repetitive spanning >128 KiB, i.e. multiple blocks /
+mixed segments) and `small_payloads()`.
+
+1. `prop_reference_encode_ruzstd_decode_roundtrip` — **crown differential
+   roundtrip**: arbitrary payload, compressed with the C encoder
+   (`zstd::stream::encode_all`, levels {1,3,6,12,19}), must decode back to the
+   exact original through `StreamingDecoder`.
+2. `prop_bulk_frame_content_size_and_decode_all` — frames with a pinned
+   Frame_Content_Size (`zstd::bulk::compress`): `FrameDecoder::content_size()`
+   must equal the original length (exercises the FCS field-width encodings,
+   incl. the 2-byte +256 rule) and `decode_all` must be lossless.
+3. `prop_arbitrary_bytes_never_panic` — **oracle-independent robustness**:
+   pure garbage, magic-prefixed garbage, and truncated-valid-frame+garbage
+   through both `StreamingDecoder` and `decode_all`; Err is fine, panic is not.
+   Output reads are capped (16 MiB) so a decompression bomb becomes a bounded
+   read instead of an OOM abort (the cap protects the test, not a contract —
+   RLE blocks can legally amplify).
+4. `prop_corrupted_frame_graceful_and_agrees_with_c` — corrupt a valid frame
+   (1–4 byte-flips, or strict truncation): ruzstd must handle it without
+   panicking, and **when both ruzstd and libzstd accept the whole corrupted
+   input they must produce identical bytes** (the format fully determines
+   decoding). Accept/reject is deliberately not compared: ruzstd defaults to a
+   100 MiB window cap (libzstd: 128 MiB), does not verify checksums, and its
+   streaming decoder stops after one frame — all documented/known divergences.
+5. `prop_skippable_frames_are_skipped` — generated skippable frames (all 16
+   magics, arbitrary lengths/payloads) interleaved with real frames:
+   `decode_all` returns exactly the concatenation of real-frame content; the C
+   decoder is run as a second witness.
+6. `prop_chunked_source_reads_equal_oneshot` — decoding through a reader that
+   returns drawn short-read chunk schedules, into drawn-size output buffers,
+   equals the one-shot decode (short-read/resume paths).
+7. `prop_decode_from_to_resumable` — the old-style push API `decode_from_to`
+   fed in drawn source-window increments with a drawn (small) target buffer
+   must make progress every step and reproduce the original (exercises the
+   header re-read and partial-block resume logic).
+8. `prop_frame_header_magic_classification` — `read_frame_header` on arbitrary
+   bytes never panics; skippable magics (0x184D2A50..=0x184D2A5F) are reported
+   as `SkipFrame` with the exact LE length; any other non-zstd magic is
+   `BadMagicNumber` with the exact value. Prefixes are boosted (uniform 4-byte
+   magics never hit the ranges).
+9. `prop_declared_window_gate` — **anti-bomb property, oracle-independent**: a
+   synthesized frame header declaring a window above the decoder's limit —
+   via the window-descriptor byte (expected size transcribed from the spec's
+   `windowLog/base/add` formula as an independent oracle) or via
+   single-segment FCS up to `u64::MAX` — must be rejected at `init`, *before*
+   any decompression; a window within the limit must be accepted (iff, both
+   directions). Boundary values around the 100 MiB limit are boosted because a
+   uniform u64 never lands there.
+
+Relation to existing fuzz targets: `decode.rs`/`decode_dict.rs` cover property
+3's no-panic core (kept there too, as in-tree shrinkable form); `interop.rs`
+covers property 1's direction plus encoder interop. New ground: corrupted-frame
+differential agreement (4), skippable-frame spec conformance (5), chunked/
+resumable API equivalence (6, 7), header classification (8), and the
+declared-window/bomb gate iff-property (9).
+
+## 3. Real Bugs Found (pinned, deliberately failing)
+
+None. No panics, no hangs, no OOMs, no differential disagreements with libzstd,
+no window-gate violations — at default and 10x case counts. No `#[ignore]`d
+reproducers were needed (no process-aborting behavior observed). The
+100 MiB-vs-128 MiB default window-limit difference against libzstd is
+documented crate behavior (`DEFAULT_MAX_WINDOW_SIZE`), not a bug, and the
+properties are written around it.
+
+## 4. Verification (Run and Reflect)
+
+- **Liveness / mutation check**: three temporary mutations — inverting the
+  roundtrip assertion (P1), inverting the assertion *inside* P4's both-accept
+  guard, and inverting the reject side of the window gate (P9) — all failed
+  with shrunk counterexamples at the default case count (e.g. P9 shrank to
+  `wd = 133` → a 104 MiB window, just past the 100 MiB limit). Mutations
+  reverted; `.hegel/` DB removed afterwards.
+- **Guarded-branch vacuity**: P4's both-accept comparison branch was counted:
+  50+ hits per 1000 cases (~5–7%), and the guard-internal mutation above
+  proved it fires (and fails) at the default count too. Not vacuous.
+- **Exploratory 10x run**: all nine properties run at `test_cases = 1000` with
+  per-test case counters printed via `--nocapture` (each counter confirmed
+  reaching 1000 — not trusted wall-clock). All green in ~3 s.
+- Final committed state: default case counts; full `cargo test -p ruzstd`
+  green — 80 lib tests (9 new) + 7 doc tests, no warnings.
+
+## 5. Exclusions, Limitations, and Follow-ups
+
+- **Dictionary decoding** is untested here beyond the existing
+  `decode_dict.rs` fuzz target and `dict_tests/` corpus; a property generating
+  valid dictionaries with the C library and round-tripping dictionary frames
+  would be a natural tenth property (needs `zstd` crate dict APIs).
+- **Checksums**: ruzstd computes but does not verify content checksums
+  (`get_calculated_checksum` is exposed; nothing compares it during decode).
+  This is why P4 only compares outputs when both decoders accept — worth an
+  upstream question, but it is visible existing behavior, not a discovered bug.
+- **Encoder**: ruzstd's own `encoding` module is only covered indirectly (the
+  existing `encode.rs`/`interop.rs` fuzz targets do this); properties here
+  focus on the decoder per the task.
+- P4's both-accept rate (~5–7%) could be raised by biasing flips into raw
+  literal regions, at the cost of generator complexity.
+- The `no_std` (`--no-default-features`) configuration is not exercised by the
+  hegel module (it is gated on `feature = "std"` because the reference oracle
+  and `std::io::Read` are needed).
